<title>USA: No threat of frost for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>No threat of frost for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The warm, high  pressure ridge centered over Brazil's coffee region is expected to remain in place through the coming weekend, Weather Services Corp said in it's daily update for Friday.</p>
<p>Colder weather has moved into Argentina, but the high pressure system already in place should prevent the cooler air from moving into Brazil's coffee regions, according to WSC.</p>
<p>Mostly fair weather was reported in the coffee belt yesterday. Temperatures remained above normal with lows ranging between 52-64 Fharenheit (11-18 Centigrade).</p>
<p>Showers are expected in southern portions of the belt during the next 24 hours. Mostly fair weather is expected elsewhere in the region through early next week. Showers may return on Tuesday or Wednesday. The lowest temperatures throughout the period will remain above 50 F (10 C).</p>
<p>&quot;There is no frost or freeze in sight,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>	 ((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
